{"name":"Bureaucracy","hex":"#746c8f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bureaucracy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Government by bureaus or their administrators or officers.","A system of administration based upon organisation into bureaus, division of labour, a hierarchy of authority, etc., designed to dispose of a large body of work in a routine manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucracy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bureaucracy","blocks":[{"text":"Bureaucracy is a system of organization where laws or regulatory authority are implemented by civil servants. Historically, a bureaucracy was a government administration managed by departments staffed with non-elected officials. Today, bureaucracy is the administrative system governing any large institution, whether publicly owned or privately owned. The public administration in many jurisdictions is an example of bureaucracy, as is any centralized hierarchical structure of an institution, including corporations, societies, nonprofit organizations, and clubs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/IRS%2C_Phila%2C_Pa.jpg/330px-IRS%2C_Phila%2C_Pa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bureaucracy","wikidata":"Q72468"},{"title":"Bureaucracy (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Bureaucracy is an interactive fiction video game released by Infocom in 1987, scripted by comic science fiction author Douglas Adams. Infocom's twenty-fourth game, it is part of the Infocom Plus range which requires a machine with a minimum of 128K of memory."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/24/Bureaucracy_box_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bureaucracy_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q304643"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Civilserviceexam1.